": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hi, \ni am trying to write a program in kotlin using the MavSdk Java Impl.\n\nI want to archieve the following scenario.\n\nMultiple drones (2 are fine to test the szenario) should connect to my program. Therefore i want to start seperate mavsdk_servers (current version 3.X.X) to connect to the drones 1 to 1.  Afterwards i connect in my kotlin program which uses java 11 (so i have to use Mavsdk Java client in version ~1.X.X) to the mavsdk servers to control the drones and to get telemetry data from them.\n\nIs that a good approach or did i missunderstood something.\n\nI am also struggling with the right setup to simulate this szenario. \nI am using px4 sitl on my wsl ubuntu instance. Is there a cleaner way to start 2 drones with diffrent ports and ips, so they can connect to the mavsdk_servers ? \n\nSorry for that maybe easy question, but i am very new to this topic.\n\nGreetings", "closed_by": {"login": "endofpen", "id": 101623754, "node_id": "U_kgDOBg6nyg", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101623754?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen", "html_url": "https://github.com/endofpen", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/endofpen/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/